    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A German-speaking merchant town under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a> law, granted self-government by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-iv-of-denmark">Eric IV of Denmark</a> in 1248.</li><li>It prospered as a Hanseatic link between Novgorod and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, governed by a council drawn from the Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">Guild</a>.</li><li>Ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and from 1346 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, it submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in 1561 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Reval's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brotherhood-of-blackheads">Brotherhood of the Blackheads</a>, an association of unmarried merchants, took its name from its patron Saint Maurice, shown as a Moor on its coat of arms.</p></aside>
    </section>

